TEXT 328 -112 Left 5 ;Three phase fault at time=2s
TEXT -536 280 Left 5 ;Busstation with three transformers \nTwo transformers for \ninitiating of the line, other lines and third \ntransformer for the load on the second bus\nis not drawn
TEXT 336 160 Left 5 ;Current inrush at 0.5s due to cable capacitances\nInrush current is capacitive (current lags voltage)\nVoltage at 2.0s decreases because of short circuit fault\nShort circuit current is inductive (current leads voltage)\n \nTry cross probing traces v(n023) und v(n024) with ALT/(ALT Gr)+Click to trace\nto see where in the circuit is the measured element
TEXT 336 16 Left 5 ;There is a line switched on for the first time at 0.5s\nThe line is switched on with two transformers in series\nwith the voltage translation factor set to their minimal value (l_=13,-13)\nTherefore if some fault arises (at t=2s) the voltage is low and impedance is\nrelative high. (Short circuit power is small)
TEXT 496 344 Left 5 ;Take also a look at the petersen \ncurrent and voltage at t=2s\nYou can see the swingin starting from 0.5 to 6s\nAt time=6s the current voltage and the currents of the\npetersen goes to zero (for both pets because of the\nsame busnames ) At 10s the fault is cleared\nand the petersen voltages and currents begun again to swingin
